CROSS-EXAMINATION TRANSCRIPT - KEY EXCERPTS

VICTIM (Prosecution Witness):

Q: You stated that you are 15 years old.
A: Yes, I am 15 years old.

Q: Which school do you attend?
A: I attend XYZ School.

Q: The school certificate produced shows your date of birth as ______.
A: Yes, that is correct.

Q: When did you join the tuition centre?
A: Six months ago.

Q: Did you ever refuse to go to tuition?
A: No, I liked going.

Q: Did the accused ever threaten you?
A: No, he never threatened me.

Q: Did you raise any alarm during the alleged incident?
A: No, I was scared.

Q: Did you tell your mother immediately?
A: Yes, I told her when I reached home.

MOTHER (Prosecution Witness):

Q: You are the mother of the victim.
A: Yes.

Q: When did the victim inform you about the incident?
A: On 05.06.2025 when she returned from tuition.

Q: Did you notice any change in her behaviour?
A: She was quiet and scared.

Q: When did you report to the police?
A: Next morning on 06.06.2025.

Q: Do you have her birth certificate?
A: No, we don't have a birth certificate.

Q: How do you know her age?
A: From her school certificate.

TUITION CENTRE STAFF (Defence Witness):

Q: You work at the tuition centre.
A: Yes.

Q: How long have you known the accused?
A: For 5 years.

Q: Is the accused a good teacher?
A: Yes, he is very respected.

Q: Have there been any complaints against him?
A: No, never.

Q: Did you ever see the victim alone with the accused?
A: Yes, during tuition hours.

Q: Did you notice anything inappropriate?
A: No, everything seemed normal.

DOCTOR (Medical Board):

Q: You conducted the ossification test.
A: Yes.

Q: What is the age range indicated?
A: Between 16 to 18 years.

Q: Can you give the exact age?
A: No, ossification can only give a range.

Q: What is the margin of error?
A: Plus or minus 2 years.

Q: Can you confirm if the victim is definitely a minor?
A: No, I cannot confirm definitively.